# 102: Test Playerbots Spawn

## Status
- [ ] Open
- [ ] In Progress
- [ ] Completed

## Current Behavior

Playerbots module is included in the build (mod-playerbots cloned during install)
but functionality has not been verified. Configuration may require adjustment.

## Intended Behavior

1. Playerbots module loads on server startup
2. Random bots spawn in world when enabled
3. Bots respond to player commands
4. Bots can be added to groups
5. Bots perform basic AI tasks (follow, assist, quest)

## Suggested Implementation Steps

1. Verify mod-playerbots compiled into worldserver
2. Check for playerbots configuration in etc/modules/
3. Enable playerbots in configuration if disabled
4. Start server and observe bot spawn messages
5. Test in-game commands: .bot add, .bot remove
6. Verify bot follows and assists player

## Configuration Options to Check

```
PlayerbotAI.Enabled = 1
PlayerbotAI.RandomBotAutologin = 1
PlayerbotAI.RandomBotCount = 100
```

## Validation Commands

```bash
# Check for playerbots config
ls -la installed-files/etc/*playerbot* 2>/dev/null || echo "No playerbot config found"

# Search for playerbots references in worldserver.conf
grep -i playerbot installed-files/etc/worldserver.conf
```

